1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,460
 Over 93% of Indian traders lose money, and I'm going to tell you exactly why.

2
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:11,240
 India's market regulators studied over 10 million people, trading futures and options.

3
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:16,440
 Futures and options are contracts that allow you to bet big on where the price is going.

4
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:20,160
 Over three years, more than 9 out of 10 of them lost money.

5
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:22,480
 Together, they lost over $20 billion.

6
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:24,620
 So who was making the money?

7
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:28,000
 Big foreign investors and professional trading firms.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,940
 And almost all of their profits came from algorithmic trading.

9
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:38,860
 Algorithmic trading means that a computer follows a set of fixed rules and places all of the trades by itself.

10
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:41,180
 No emotions and no guessing.

11
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:46,880
 Imagine playing chess against a computer while you're tired, angry and in a hurry.

12
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:50,700
 You're the tired player and the computer is the trading algorithm.

13
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:53,840
 It never gets tired and it never gets mad.

14
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,100
 That's what regular traders in India were up against.

15
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:00,420
 And more than 9 out of 10 of them lost their money.

16
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:03,680
 You can never beat a machine just by guessing harder.

17
00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:07,220
 You need rules too, and you need to test them on past prices.

18
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:13,600
 If you're interested in algo trading, comment cube and I'll send you the full breakdown on exactly how to start.

